7: #               pool means the next database-needing item is REJECTED at start, never queued.
8: #   OCCUPIED  - the harness runner takes the slot for each verify window, and releases it in a
9: #               finally. That claim is written by tests/at/harness/db-pool.ts, not by this file.
10: #   released  - the coordinator deletes the reservation at the item sweep.
