THER THAN ONLY RESET. Auth reads config.toml when its\n16: # container is created. The stack that was already running was created BEFORE this branch flipped\n17: # [auth.email] enable_confirmations to true, and its container proved it - the reading is the\n18: # first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n19: # check in step 5 would have measured the OLD setting.\n20: \n21: ===== BEFORE: the running auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true means confirmations are OFF =====\n22: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n23: \n24: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n25: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n26: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n27: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n28: \n29: ===== bun run db:stop =====\n30: $ bun run db:stop\n31: bun : $ bunx supabase stop\n32: At line:1 char:1\n33: + bun run db:stop\n34: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n35:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase stop:String) [], RemoteException\n36:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n37:  \n38: {\"project_id_filter\":\"poancmeitlmxejofwzuu\",\"backup\":true,\"message\":\"Stopped supabase local development setup.\"}\n39: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n40: \n41: ===== bun run db:start - the stack comes back up, and its auth container is created from THIS branch's config.toml =====\n42: $ bun run db:start\n43: bun : $ bunx supabase start\n44: At line:1 char:1\n45: + bun run db:start\n46: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n47:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase start:String) [], RemoteException\n48:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n49:  \n50: {\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\",\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-publishable-key>\",\"SECRET_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-secret-key>\",\"JWT_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED-local-jwt-secret>\",\"ANON_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"MAILPIT_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"INBUCKET_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"STORAGE_S3_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\":\"local\",\"message\":\"\"}\n51: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n52: \n53: ===== AFTER: the NEW auth container's confirmation setting - GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false means confirmations are ON =====\n54: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n55: \n56: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n57: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n58: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false\n59: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n60: \n61: # MEASURED, AND NOT WHAT THE FILE SAYS: the auth container carries\n62: # GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000 while supabase/config.toml carries [auth.rate_limit]\n63: # email_sent = 2. The CLI did not push the file's value into the container. So the checked-in\n64: # number is NOT the cap this run measures against. Step 5 check (f) reports the file's value and\n65: # whether the mailer actually refused anything; this line records why those two can disagree.\n66: \n67: ===== bun run db:reset =====\n68: $ bun run db:reset\n69: bun : $ bunx supabase db reset\n70: At line:1 char:1\n71: + bun run db:reset\n72: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n73:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: ($ bunx supabase db reset:String) [], RemoteException\n74:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n75:  \n76: Resetting local database...\n77: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\n78: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET\n79: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\n80: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_SECRET\n81: Recreating database...\n82: Initialising schema...\n83: Seeding globals from roles.sql...\n84: Skipping migration .gitkeep... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\n85: Skipping migration README.md... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\n86: Applying migration 20260808120000_accounts_org_membership_and_acknowledgments.sql...\n87: Applying migration 20260809090000_volunteer_github_link_and_imported_profile.sql...\n88: WARN: no files matched pattern: supabase/seed.sql\n89: Skipping migration .gitkeep... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\n90: Skipping migration README.md... (file name must match pattern \"<timestamp>_name.sql\")\n91: Restarting containers...\n92: A new version of Supabase CLI is available: v2.113.0 (currently installed v2.110.0)\n93: We recommend updating regularly for new features and bug fixes: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/cli/getting-started#updating-the-supabase-cli\n94: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\n95: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GOOGLE_SECRET\n96: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID\n97: WARN: environment variable is unset: SUPABASE_AUTH_EXTERNAL_GITHUB_SECRET\n98: A new version of Supabase CLI is available: v2.113.0 (currently installed v2.110.0)\n99: We recommend updating regularly for new features and bug fixes: https://supabase.com/docs/guides/cli/getting-started#updating-the-supabase-cli\n100: Finished \u001b[36msupabase db reset\u001b[39m on branch \u001b[36mmain\u001b[39m.\n101: {\"target\":\"local\",\"version\":\"\",\"message\":\"Reset local database.\"}\n102: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n103: \n104: ===== bunx supabase status - the stack is up after the reset =====\n105: $ bunx supabase status\n106: bunx : Stopped services: [supabase_imgproxy_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu supabase_pooler_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu]\n107: At line:1 char:1\n108: + bunx supabase status\n109: + ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n110:     + CategoryInfo          : NotSpecified: (Stopped service...eitlmxejofwzuu]:String) [], RemoteException\n111:     + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NativeCommandError\n112:  \n113: {\"DB_URL\":\"postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres\",\"API_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321\",\"REST_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/rest/v1\",\"GRAPHQL_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/graphql/v1\",\"FUNCTIONS_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1\",\"MCP_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/mcp\",\"STUDIO_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54323\",\"PUBLISHABLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-publishable-key>\",\"SECRET_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-secret-key>\",\"JWT_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED-local-jwt-secret>\",\"ANON_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"SERVICE_ROLE_KEY\":\"<REDACTED-local-demo-jwt>\",\"MAILPIT_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"INBUCKET_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54324\",\"STORAGE_S3_URL\":\"http://127.0.0.1:54321/storage/v1/s3\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_ID\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_ACCESS_KEY_SECRET\":\"<REDACTED>\",\"S3_PROTOCOL_REGION\":\"local\",\"message\":\"\"}\n114: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n115: \n116: ===== the auth container AFTER the reset, re-read - the flip survives the container restart =====\n117: $ docker inspect supabase_auth_poancmeitlmxejofwzuu --format '{{range .Config.Env}}{{println .}}{{end}}' | Select-String -Pattern \"AUTOCONFIRM|RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL\"\n118: \n119: GOTRUE_RATE_LIMIT_EMAIL_SENT=360000\n120: GOTRUE_SMS_AUTOCONFIRM=true\n121: GOTRUE_MAILER_AUTOCONFIRM=false\n122: ----- exit code: 0 -----\n123: \n124: ===== bunx supabase functions serve - THE OPERATOR-SIDE BINDING OF THE MOUNT TO THIS WORKTREE =====\n125: # Gate 2 ruling [A5] asks for this record, and this is it. The stale-mount probe inside\n126: # proof-local.ts can tell REACHABILITY from a 404; it cannot tell WHICH directory the edge runtime\n127: # mounted. So the launch is written down instead of inferred.\n128: #\n129: # COMMAND: bunx supabase functions serve\n130: # WORKING DIRECTORY: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n131: # FLAGS: none. --no-verify-jwt is NOT passed, so the runtime verifies the caller's token exactly as\n132: #        it would in a deployment.\n133: # LAUNCHED: 2026-08-09 18:31:36 +03:00\n134: # PROCESS ID: 49328\n135: #\n136: # Its first lines of output, which name the two functions it mounted:\n137: 2026-08-09T15:30:55.680974747Z Serving functions on http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/<function-name>\n138: 2026-08-09T15:30:55.681020066Z  - http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/complete-signup\n139: 2026-08-09T15:30:55.681022631Z  - http://127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/create-organization\n140: 2026-08-09T15:30:55.681024475Z Using supabase-edge-runtime-1.74.2 (compatible with Deno v2.1.4)\n141: #\n142: # And the probe the proof script performs, run here by hand as well: an unauthenticated POST to\n143: # complete-signup answers HTTP 401 - a refusal, not a 404, so the function is being served.\n144: #\n145: # WHY THE MOUNT'S REVISION IS NOT LOAD-BEARING, verified in the tree before this run:\n146: #   git diff main...HEAD --stat -- supabase/functions/\n147: #     supabase/functions/_shared/verification.ts | 167 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n148: #     1 file changed, 167 insertions(+)\n149: #   complete-signup/index.ts imports only _shared/accounts.ts, _shared/github.ts and _shared/edge.ts.\n150: # This branch therefore changes nothing complete-signup imports, and every revision it could be\n151: # compared against is byte for byte the same code.\n152: #\n153: # STOPPED AFTER STEP 5 FINISHED, on purpose. A `functions serve` left alive against a worktree that\n154: # is later removed is the exact stale-mount hazard this file's own comment describes, and this item\n155: # has no further use for it: nothing else in the item calls an edge function, and continuous\n156: # integration has no database. The edge runtime CONTAINER that `supabase start` runs stays up and\n157: # still answers 401, which is the stack's normal state and not this launch.\n158: ----- the serve process was stopped by the executor after step 5 -----\n\n(End of file - total 158 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# AI4DEV-59 (email verification, unverified-write gate) - STEP 4: THE STACK WITH THE FLIPPED CONFIG\n# Started: 2026-08-09 18:27:51 +03:00\n# Worktree: C:\\Users\\nirdr\\Downloads\\ai4good\\.claude\\worktrees\\agent-aa95110cbeab31aa7\n# Branch:   nirdrang/ai4dev-59-email-verification-and-the-gate-on-unverified-writing-d2l1\n#\n# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT KEYS ARE REDACTED BELOW, exactly as the predecessor item's stack-up\n# transcript redacts them. They are local-stack values reachable only at 127.0.0.1 on the\n# machine that ran this, and nothing key-shaped is committed. GitHub push protection once\n# REFUSED a push in this project for exactly this file's predecessor, so the rule has a\n# mechanical enforcer. What is redacted: the publishable key, the secret key, the local JWT\n# signing secret, both demo JWTs (anon and service role) and the two S3 protocol credentials.\n# What is NOT redacted, because none of it is a credential: every URL and port, and the\n# postgres/postgres local database URL the Supabase CLI prints on every machine.\n#\n# WHY THE STACK IS STOPPED AND STARTED RATHER THAN ONLY RESET. Auth reads config.toml when its\n# container is created. The stack that was already running was created BEFORE this branch flipped\n# [auth.email] enable_confirmations to true, and its container proved it - the reading is the\n# first command below. A db reset alone would have left that container in place, and every\n# check in step 5 